  ],
  "slug": "automated-microscopy-2e31",
  "summary": "TISCH3, a 42-cancer TME atlas and PDAC BioPortal expand tumour single-cell and spatial resources, while new methods add spatial context and multimodal fusion.",
  "synthesis": "The dominant thread is the consolidation of tumour transcriptomic data into public, queryable resources, with spatial data increasingly built into the analysis layer. TISCH3 grows to 477 datasets, adding 218 scRNA-seq and 69 spatial transcriptomics collections with spatial analysis tools. A pan-cancer single-cell screen across 42 cancers reports tumour microenvironment programs conserved across organs and species, and releases an atlas with scTME software. PDAC BioPortal combines bulk, single-nucleus and spatial pancreatic cohorts with pathway and survival tools. DriverDBv5 and X-BCRdb extend the resource layer to multi-omics driver genes and BCR-paired single-cell clonotype–transcriptome data. Methods target analytical gaps. SpaceMACE adds spatial information to tumour-cell annotation alongside CNV inference, and HIT-Fuse applies hierarchical tensor fusion to six omics and pathomics modalities while handling missing modalities. A Cell Reports study on genomic burden and selection in genetic immune escape across cancers is related but less directly tied to resource building.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-opus-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-11-23"
}
